        "id": 48,
        "title": "Rotate Image",
        "category": "Greedy & Math",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>You are given an <code>n x n</code> 2D <code>matrix</code> representing an image, rotate the image by <strong>90</strong> degrees (clockwise).</p>\n\n<p>You have to rotate the image <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In-place_algorithm\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>in-place</strong></a>, which means you have to modify the input 2D matrix directly. <strong>DO NOT</strong> allocate another 2D matrix and do the rotation.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/08/28/mat1.jpg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 188px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">matrix = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[[7,4,1],[8,5,2],[9,6,3]]</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/08/28/mat2.jpg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 201px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">matrix = [[5,1,9,11],[2,4,8,10],[13,3,6,7],[15,14,12,16]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[[15,13,2,5],[14,3,4,1],[12,6,8,9],[16,7,10,11]]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>n == matrix.length == matrix[i].length</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 20</code></li>\n\t<li><code>-1000 &lt;= matrix[i][j] &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n</ul>",
