        "category": "Linked List",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>Given a binary tree</p>\n\n<pre>\nstruct Node {\n  int val;\n  Node *left;\n  Node *right;\n  Node *next;\n}\n</pre>\n\n<p>Populate each next pointer to point to its next right node. If there is no next right node, the next pointer should be set to <code>NULL</code>.</p>\n\n<p>Initially, all next pointers are set to <code>NULL</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2019/02/15/117_sample.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 171px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">root = [1,2,3,4,5,null,7]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[1,#,2,3,#,4,5,7,#]</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">root = []</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[0, 6000]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-100 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #a855f7; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-rocket\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Follow-up Challenge:</div></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>You may only use constant extra space.</li>\n\t<li>The recursive approach is fine. You may assume implicit stack space does not count as extra space for this problem.</li>\n</ul>",
        "companies": [
            "Amazon",
            "Bloomberg",
            "Google",
            "Meta",
            "Microsoft",
            "Snowflake",
            "Uber"
        ],
        "tags": [
            "Linked List",
            "Tree",
            "Depth-First Search",
            "Breadth-First Search",
            "Binary Tree"
        ],
        "constraints": [
            "The number of nodes in the tree is in the range [0, 6000].",
            "-100 <= Node.val <= 100"
        ],
        "hints": [
            "Use a dummy head node (sentinel node) to dramatically simplify edge cases involving inserting or deleting at the head.",
            "For pointer manipulations (reversing, swapping), maintain distinct pointers for previous, current, and next nodes.",
            "Use the Fast and Slow pointer technique (Floyd's Cycle Detection) for finding midpoints or detecting cycles in O(1) space."
        ],
        "optimalComplexity": {
            "time": "O(N)",
            "space": "O(1)"
        },
