        "description": "<div style=\"background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.25); border-left: 3px solid #2ed573; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #cbd5e1;\"><strong style=\"color: #2ed573;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Beginner Tip:</strong> Use recursion (DFS) to explore paths deeply, or a queue (BFS) to process nodes level by level.</div><p>Given the <code>root</code> of a binary tree, return <em>the preorder traversal of its nodes&#39; values</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,null,2,3]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[1,2,3]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2024/08/29/screenshot-2024-08-29-202743.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 264px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,2,3,4,5,null,8,null,null,6,7,9]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[1,2,4,5,6,7,3,8,9]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2024/08/29/tree_2.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 286px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[0, 100]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-100 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #a855f7; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-rocket\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Follow-up Challenge:</div> Recursive solution is trivial, could you do it iteratively?</p>",
