        "description": "<p>Given an <code>m x n</code> <code>board</code>&nbsp;of characters and a list of strings <code>words</code>, return <em>all words on the board</em>.</p>\n\n<p>Each word must be constructed from letters of sequentially adjacent cells, where <strong>adjacent cells</strong> are horizontally or vertically neighboring. The same letter cell may not be used more than once in a word.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/11/07/search1.jpg\" style=\"width: 322px; height: 322px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">board = [[&quot;o&quot;,&quot;a&quot;,&quot;a&quot;,&quot;n&quot;],[&quot;e&quot;,&quot;t&quot;,&quot;a&quot;,&quot;e&quot;],[&quot;i&quot;,&quot;h&quot;,&quot;k&quot;,&quot;r&quot;],[&quot;i&quot;,&quot;f&quot;,&quot;l&quot;,&quot;v&quot;]], words = [&quot;oath&quot;,&quot;pea&quot;,&quot;eat&quot;,&quot;rain&quot;]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[&quot;eat&quot;,&quot;oath&quot;]</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/11/07/search2.jpg\" style=\"width: 162px; height: 162px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">board = [[&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;],[&quot;c&quot;,&quot;d&quot;]], words = [&quot;abcb&quot;]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>m == board.length</code></li>\n\t<li><code>n == board[i].length</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= m, n &lt;= 12</code></li>\n\t<li><code>board[i][j]</code> is a lowercase English letter.</li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= words.length &lt;= 3 * 10<sup>4</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= words[i].length &lt;= 10</code></li>\n\t<li><code>words[i]</code> consists of lowercase English letters.</li>\n\t<li>All the strings of <code>words</code> are unique.</li>\n</ul>",
