        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "description": "<div style=\"background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.25); border-left: 3px solid #2ed573; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #cbd5e1;\"><strong style=\"color: #2ed573;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Beginner Tip:</strong> Use recursion (DFS) to explore paths deeply, or a queue (BFS) to process nodes level by level.</div><p>Given the <code>root</code> of a binary tree, invert the tree, and return <em>its root</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/14/invert1-tree.jpg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 165px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">root = [4,2,7,1,3,6,9]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[4,7,2,9,6,3,1]</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/14/invert2-tree.jpg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 120px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">root = [2,1,3]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[2,3,1]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[0, 100]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-100 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>",
