        "category": "Stack & Queue",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "description": "<div style=\"background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.25); border-left: 3px solid #2ed573; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #cbd5e1;\"><strong style=\"color: #2ed573;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Beginner Tip:</strong> Use a stack (last-in, first-out) for matching brackets or reverse order tracking.</div><p>Given a string <code>s</code>, find the <strong>first</strong> non-repeating character in it and return its index. If it <strong>does not</strong> exist, return <code>-1</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;skilmatrix&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">0</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>The character <code>&#39;l&#39;</code> at index 0 is the first character that does not occur at any other index.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">s = &quot;loveskilmatrix&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">2</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>s</code> consists of only lowercase English letters.</li>\n</ul>",
