        "category": "Dynamic Programming",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>You are given an array of binary strings <code>strs</code> and two integers <code>m</code> and <code>n</code>.</p>\n\n<p>Return <em>the size of the largest subset of <code>strs</code> such that there are <strong>at most</strong> </em><code>m</code><em> </em><code>0</code><em>&#39;s and </em><code>n</code><em> </em><code>1</code><em>&#39;s in the subset</em>.</p>\n\n<p>A set <code>x</code> is a <strong>subset</strong> of a set <code>y</code> if all elements of <code>x</code> are also elements of <code>y</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">strs = [&quot;10&quot;,&quot;0001&quot;,&quot;111001&quot;,&quot;1&quot;,&quot;0&quot;], m = 5, n = 3</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">4</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> The largest subset with at most 5 0&#39;s and 3 1&#39;s is {&quot;10&quot;, &quot;0001&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, &quot;0&quot;}, so the answer is 4.</div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">strs = [&quot;10&quot;,&quot;0&quot;,&quot;1&quot;], m = 1, n = 1</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">2</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= strs.length &lt;= 600</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= strs[i].length &lt;= 100</code></li>\n\t<li><code>strs[i]</code> consists only of digits <code>&#39;0&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;1&#39;</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= m, n &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>",
