        "id": 720,
        "title": "Longest Word in Dictionary",
        "category": "Trie & Prefix Tree",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>Given an array of strings <code>words</code> representing an English Dictionary, return <em>the longest word in</em> <code>words</code> <em>that can be built one character at a time by other words in</em> <code>words</code>.</p>\n\n<p>If there is more than one possible answer, return the longest word with the smallest lexicographical order. If there is no answer, return the empty string.</p>\n\n<p>Note that the word should be built from left to right with each additional character being added to the end of a previous word.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">words = [&quot;w&quot;,&quot;wo&quot;,&quot;wor&quot;,&quot;worl&quot;,&quot;world&quot;]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">&quot;world&quot;</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> The word &quot;world&quot; can be built one character at a time by &quot;w&quot;, &quot;wo&quot;, &quot;wor&quot;, and &quot;worl&quot;.</div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">words = [&quot;a&quot;,&quot;banana&quot;,&quot;app&quot;,&quot;appl&quot;,&quot;ap&quot;,&quot;apply&quot;,&quot;apple&quot;]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">&quot;apple&quot;</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> Both &quot;apply&quot; and &quot;apple&quot; can be built from other words in the dictionary. However, &quot;apple&quot; is lexicographically smaller than &quot;apply&quot;.</div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= words.length &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= words[i].length &lt;= 30</code></li>\n\t<li><code>words[i]</code> consists of lowercase English letters.</li>\n</ul>",
