        "id": 844,
        "title": "Backspace String Compare",
        "category": "Two Pointers",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "description": "<div style=\"background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.25); border-left: 3px solid #2ed573; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #cbd5e1;\"><strong style=\"color: #2ed573;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Beginner Tip:</strong> Place one pointer at the start and one at the end, moving them toward each other based on the target condition.</div><p>Given two strings <code>s</code> and <code>t</code>, return <code>true</code> <em>if they are equal when both are typed into empty text editors</em>. <code>&#39;#&#39;</code> means a backspace character.</p>\n\n<p>Note that after backspacing an empty text, the text will continue empty.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">s = &quot;ab#c&quot;, t = &quot;ad#c&quot;</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">true</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> Both s and t become &quot;ac&quot;.</div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">s = &quot;ab##&quot;, t = &quot;c#d#&quot;</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">true</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> Both s and t become &quot;&quot;.</div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code><span>1 &lt;= s.length, t.length &lt;= 200</span></code></li>\n\t<li><span><code>s</code> and <code>t</code> only contain lowercase letters and <code>&#39;#&#39;</code> characters.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #a855f7; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-rocket\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Follow-up Challenge:</div> Can you solve it in <code>O(n)</code> time and <code>O(1)</code> space?</p>",
