        "id": 1557,
        "title": "Minimum Number of Vertices to Reach All Nodes",
        "category": "Trees & Graphs",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>Given a<strong>&nbsp;directed acyclic graph</strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;<code>n</code>&nbsp;vertices numbered from&nbsp;<code>0</code>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<code>n-1</code>,&nbsp;and an array&nbsp;<code>edges</code>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<code>edges[i] = [from<sub>i</sub>, to<sub>i</sub>]</code>&nbsp;represents a directed edge from node&nbsp;<code>from<sub>i</sub></code>&nbsp;to node&nbsp;<code>to<sub>i</sub></code>.</p>\n\n<p>Find <em>the smallest set of vertices from which all nodes in the graph are reachable</em>. It&#39;s guaranteed that a unique solution exists.</p>\n\n<p>Notice that you can return the vertices in any order.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/07/07/untitled22.png\" style=\"width: 231px; height: 181px;\" /></p>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">n = 6, edges = [[0,1],[0,2],[2,5],[3,4],[4,2]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[0,3]</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/07/07/untitled.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 201px;\" /></p>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[2,1],[3,1],[1,4],[2,4]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[0,2,3]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>2 &lt;= n &lt;= 10^5</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= edges.length &lt;= min(10^5, n * (n - 1) / 2)</code></li>\n\t<li><code>edges[i].length == 2</code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= from<sub>i,</sub>&nbsp;to<sub>i</sub> &lt; n</code></li>\n\t<li>All pairs <code>(from<sub>i</sub>, to<sub>i</sub>)</code> are distinct.</li>\n</ul>",
