        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "description": "<div style=\"background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.25); border-left: 3px solid #2ed573; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 13px; color: #cbd5e1;\"><strong style=\"color: #2ed573;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-lightbulb\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Beginner Tip:</strong> Start by checking simple edge cases. Use a hash map or set to check for complements in a single loop without nested checking!</div><p>Given an array of positive integers <code>arr</code>, find a pattern of length <code>m</code> that is repeated <code>k</code> or more times.</p>\n\n<p>A <strong>pattern</strong> is a subarray (consecutive sub-sequence) that consists of one or more values, repeated multiple times <strong>consecutively </strong>without overlapping. A pattern is defined by its length and the number of repetitions.</p>\n\n<p>Return <code>true</code> <em>if there exists a pattern of length</em> <code>m</code> <em>that is repeated</em> <code>k</code> <em>or more times, otherwise return</em> <code>false</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">arr = [1,2,4,4,4,4], m = 1, k = 3</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">true</code></div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">arr = [1,2,1,2,1,1,1,3], m = 2, k = 2</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">true</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p><div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>2 &lt;= arr.length &lt;= 100</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= arr[i] &lt;= 100</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= m &lt;= 100</code></li>\n\t<li><code>2 &lt;= k &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>",
