        "title": "Checking Existence of Edge Length Limited Paths",
        "category": "Advanced Graphs & Union-Find",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "description": "<p>An undirected graph of <code>n</code> nodes is defined by <code>edgeList</code>, where <code>edgeList[i] = [u<sub>i</sub>, v<sub>i</sub>, dis<sub>i</sub>]</code> denotes an edge between nodes <code>u<sub>i</sub></code> and <code>v<sub>i</sub></code> with distance <code>dis<sub>i</sub></code>. Note that there may be <strong>multiple</strong> edges between two nodes.</p>\n\n<p>Given an array <code>queries</code>, where <code>queries[j] = [p<sub>j</sub>, q<sub>j</sub>, limit<sub>j</sub>]</code>, your task is to determine for each <code>queries[j]</code> whether there is a path between <code>p<sub>j</sub></code> and <code>q<sub>j</sub></code><sub> </sub>such that each edge on the path has a distance <strong>strictly less than</strong> <code>limit<sub>j</sub></code> .</p>\n\n<p>Return <em>a <strong>boolean array</strong> </em><code>answer</code><em>, where </em><code>answer.length == queries.length</code> <em>and the </em><code>j<sup>th</sup></code> <em>value of </em><code>answer</code> <em>is </em><code>true</code><em> if there is a path for </em><code>queries[j]</code><em> is </em><code>true</code><em>, and </em><code>false</code><em> otherwise</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/12/08/h.png\" style=\"width: 267px; height: 262px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">n = 3, edgeList = [[0,1,2],[1,2,4],[2,0,8],[1,0,16]], queries = [[0,1,2],[0,2,5]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[false,true]</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> The above figure shows the given graph. Note that there are two overlapping edges between 0 and 1 with distances 2 and 16.</div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/12/08/q.png\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 358px;\" />\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">n = 5, edgeList = [[0,1,10],[1,2,5],[2,3,9],[3,4,13]], queries = [[0,4,14],[1,4,13]]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[true,false]</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> The above figure shows the given graph.</div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>2 &lt;= n &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= edgeList.length, queries.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>edgeList[i].length == 3</code></li>\n\t<li><code>queries[j].length == 3</code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= u<sub>i</sub>, v<sub>i</sub>, p<sub>j</sub>, q<sub>j</sub> &lt;= n - 1</code></li>\n\t<li><code>u<sub>i</sub> != v<sub>i</sub></code></li>\n\t<li><code>p<sub>j</sub> != q<sub>j</sub></code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= dis<sub>i</sub>, limit<sub>j</sub> &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n\t<li>There may be <strong>multiple</strong> edges between two nodes.</li>\n</ul>",
