        "id": 2411,
        "title": "Smallest Subarrays With Maximum Bitwise OR",
        "category": "Binary Search",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "description": "<p>You are given a <strong>0-indexed</strong> array <code>nums</code> of length <code>n</code>, consisting of non-negative integers. For each index <code>i</code> from <code>0</code> to <code>n - 1</code>, you must determine the size of the <strong>minimum sized</strong> non-empty subarray of <code>nums</code> starting at <code>i</code> (<strong>inclusive</strong>) that has the <strong>maximum</strong> possible <strong>bitwise OR</strong>.</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>In other words, let <code>B<sub>ij</sub></code> be the bitwise OR of the subarray <code>nums[i...j]</code>. You need to find the smallest subarray starting at <code>i</code>, such that bitwise OR of this subarray is equal to <code>max(B<sub>ik</sub>)</code> where <code>i &lt;= k &lt;= n - 1</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The bitwise OR of an array is the bitwise OR of all the numbers in it.</p>\n\n<p>Return <em>an integer array </em><code>answer</code><em> of size </em><code>n</code><em> where </em><code>answer[i]</code><em> is the length of the <strong>minimum</strong> sized subarray starting at </em><code>i</code><em> with <strong>maximum</strong> bitwise OR.</em></p>\n\n<p>A <strong>subarray</strong> is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 1:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">nums = [1,0,2,1,3]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[3,3,2,2,1]</code></div><div style=\"color: #a1a1aa; font-size: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);\"><b>Explanation:</b> The maximum possible bitwise OR starting at any index is 3.</div></div>\n\n<div style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; color: #38bdf8; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Example 2:</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #090d16; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-left: 3px solid #38bdf8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 6px 0 16px 0; color: #e2e8f0;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 6px;\"><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Input:</span> <code style=\"color: #38bdf8; background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">nums = [1,2]</code></div><div><span style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 600;\">Output:</span> <code style=\"color: #2ed573; background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.08); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;\">[2,1]</code></div></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div style=\"font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: #ffc01e; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation\" style=\"margin-right:6px;\"></i>Constraints:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>n == nums.length</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>0 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup></code></li>\n</ul>",
        "companies": [
            "Amazon",
            "Bloomberg",
            "Google",
            "Meta",
            "Microsoft"
        ],
        "tags": [
            "Array",
            "Binary Search",
            "Bit Manipulation",
            "Sliding Window"
        ],
        "constraints": [
            "n == nums.length",
            "1 <= n <= 105",
            "0 <= nums[i] <= 109"
        ],
        "hints": [
            "Consider trying to solve the problem for each bit position separately.",
            "For each bit position, find the position of the next number that has a 1 in that position, if any.",
            "Take the maximum distance to such a number, including the current number."
        ],
